From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: John Doe <john.doe@somewhere.on.planet>
Date: Sat, 5 Sep 2026 12:00:00 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] JM10 boot-from-external: enable sata0 + combphy0_ps in the U-Boot control DT

Part of the optional JM10_BOOT_EXTERNAL mode: keep a full OS on an
external USB2 / mSATA disk and boot it from an eMMC that carries only
the bootloader. Apply together with the sibling boot-ext patches.

Signed-off-by: John Doe <john.doe@somewhere.on.planet>
---
 arch/arm/dts/rk3588-u-boot.dtsi | 11 +
 1 file changed, 11 insertions(+)

diff --git a/arch/arm/dts/rk3588-u-boot.dtsi b/arch/arm/dts/rk3588-u-boot.dtsi
index 8ae5088d478e..8ae5088d478e 100644
--- a/arch/arm/dts/rk3588-u-boot.dtsi
+++ b/arch/arm/dts/rk3588-u-boot.dtsi
@@ -285,3 +285,14 @@
 {
 	u-boot,dm-spl;
 };
+/* JM10 boot-from-external: enable SATA0 (mSATA) with combphy0_ps for SCSI
+ * boot. The RK3588_PD_PHP power-domains reference is inert here (U-Boot has
+ * no RK3588 power-domain driver; PHP is powered at reset). */
+&sata0 {
+	status = "okay";
+};
+
+&combphy0_ps {
+	status = "okay";
+};
+
-- 
